can you explain how the strategy patter work, and give me an example

------------AI Response------------
Strategy Pattern — super simple

The Strategy Pattern is used when you have different ways to do the same thing.

For example, a delivery app can deliver by:

🚗 Car
🏍️ Bike
🚲 Bicycle

Instead of putting everything in one big class, we create separate strategies:

interface DeliveryStrategy {
    void deliver();
}

class CarDelivery implements DeliveryStrategy {
    public void deliver() {
        System.out.println("Deliver by car");
    }
}

class BikeDelivery implements DeliveryStrategy {
    public void deliver() {
        System.out.println("Deliver by bike");
    }
}

Then we choose which strategy to use:

DeliveryStrategy strategy = new BikeDelivery();
strategy.deliver();

In short:
👉 Strategy Pattern = choose between different behaviors without changing the main class.

